      "description": "The Scala Data Centers Tambore Campus, located in Barueri, Brazil, stands as the largest and most advanced data center campus in Latin America. With a planned total capacity of 600 MW distributed across several data centers, this complex represents a significant investment in Brazil's digital infrastructure.  A core principle of the Tambore Campus is its commitment to sustainability, operating on 100% renewable energy sourced through long-term Power Purchase Agreements (PPAs) that support the development of new wind and solar farms.  The campus achieves exceptional energy efficiency with a Power Usage Effectiveness (PUE) of 1.35, significantly outperforming the global average. This efficiency is bolstered by the implementation of advanced liquid cooling systems.  Furthermore, Scala prioritizes responsible water management by utilizing closed-loop cooling systems, which eliminate any reliance on local groundwater or aquifers.",
